mil:AirForceStationRAF void:inDataset mil:datasetdefinition;
                       a skos:Concept,
                         owl:Class;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                       rdfs:label "Royal Air Force station"@en;
                       owl:sameAs resource:Royal_Air_Force_station;
                       owl:subClass mil:AirForceStation;
                       skos:definition "A Royal Air Force station is a permanent Royal Air Force operations location. Many RAF stations are aerodromes, or airbases, being the home to one or more flying squadrons. Other RAF stations are training units, administrative units, headquarters (HQ), or carry out ground-based operational tasks. Although many RAF units are often called stations, they can only be properly classified as an RAF station if they are self-accounting with their own station commander and headquarters."@en;
                       org:unitOf mil:AirForceGroup;
                       foaf:name "Royal Air Force station".
