mil:Rank_Ferik void:inDataset mil:datasetdefinition;
               a skos:Concept,
                 mil:MilitaryRank;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
               rdfs:label "Ferik (rank)"@en;
               owl:sameAs resource:Ferik_%28rank%29;
               skos:definition """Ferik was a military rank of the Ottoman Army. It is translated as Major General or Lieutenant General (Korgeneral). It was superior to a Mirliva (\"Brigadier\") and junior to a Birinci Ferik (\"First Ferik/General\"). The title of Ferik was abolished with Act No. 2590 of 26 November 1934 on the Abolition of Titles and Appellations such as Efendi, Bey or Pasha."""@en;
               foaf:name "Ferik".
