                owl:sameAs resource:Hetman;
                skos:definition """Hetman was the title of the second-highest military commander in 15th- to 18th-century Poland and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, which together, from 1569 to 1795, comprised the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, or Rzeczpospolita. \"Hetman\" was also the highest military office, and head of state, in Ukraine's Cossack Hetmanate. The title (Ð³ÐµÑÑÐ¼Ð°Ð½) was used by Ukraine's Cossacks from the 16th century, and by the Czechs (hejtman) in Bohemia from the Hussite Wars (15th century) on."""@en;
                foaf:name "Hetman".
