mil:Rank_Sergeant_Pilot void:inDataset mil:datasetdefinition;
                        a skos:Concept,
                          mil:MilitaryRank;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                        rdfs:label "Fältflygare"@sv,
                                   "Sergeant Pilot"@en;
                        owl:sameAs resource:Sergeant_Pilot;
                        skos:definition "A Sergeant Pilot was a non-commissioned officer who had undergone flight training and was a qualified pilot in the air forces of several Commonwealth countries and in the United States Army Air Force before, during and after World War II. After World War II, non-commissioned pilots began to be phased out and today all air force pilots are commissioned officers. In the United States, the Flight Officer Act ended enlisted men's chances of undergoing flight training."@en;
                        foaf:name "Sergeant Pilot".
