mil:Rank_Vice-Admiral_of_the_West void:inDataset mil:datasetdefinition;
                                  a skos:Concept,
                                    mil:MilitaryRank;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                                  rdfs:label "Vice-Admiral of the West"@en;
                                  owl:sameAs resource:Vice-Admiral_of_the_West;
                                  skos:definition "The historical title Vice-Admiral of the West is sometimes applied to holders of the crown appointment Vice-Admiral of the Coast of counties in the South West of England. The duties of a Vice-Admiral of the coast were to control the shipping (especially piracy) around a maritime county's coast and organise defense on land and at sea. He also acted as a local judge to deal with maritime matters."@en;
                                  foaf:name "Vice-Admiral of the West".
